 ;; PROFILES/TIMING (ms) -------------------------------------------------------
 ;; If defining a profile we need all four timings here (in ms) otherwise they
 ;; get compuled to null.
 ;; Default values are alone=1000, held=500, delay=500, sim=50,
 ;; simlayer-threshold=250

 :profiles {:Default {:default true
                      :alone 500   ; pressed for <300ms = a tapped key
                      :held 500   ; pressed for >500s = a held key
                      :delay 300   ; :delayed (invoked/canceled) actions time
                      :sim 50}}  ; keys pressed together within <50ms = chord

 :simlayer-threshold 250 ; top level only; silently ignored inside :profiles

 ;; LAYERS ---------------------------------------------------------------------
 ;; Goku supports two types of builtin layers: simlayers and layers.
 ;; * simlayers are fast, simultaneous press type layers
 ;; * layers are more hold and pick the key type
 ;; In each case modifiers get dropped so I construct a couple layers manually
 ;; in order to pass through modifiers (currently things like shift in the case
 ;; of universal-sidebar below (there may be other instances of modifier pass
 ;; through), so if I stop using modifier pass through or reconfigure how the
 ;; the secondary layers (quit/open) work there then maybe I'll revert to
 ;; regular layers for goku consistency. Not really important to do though, I
 ;; don't think. No obvious downside of my handling layers "manually" like this.
 ;;
 ;; Basically in those manually configured layers (opsmode, wmmode which is
 ;; currently merged with opsmode but easily separated back out) I set a "layer"
 ;; variable on press, clear it on release. alone=normal key tap.
 ;;
 ;; caps lock as layer activator is my daily driver and primary mod key.
 ;; I also lean on it to do window management for omniwm (currentl wm of choice)
 ;;
 ;;   caps lock (hold) = wm-mode      : window navigation + open apps (tap = esc)
 ;;   tab       (hold) = wm-mode-alt  : window movement + new windows (tap = tab)

